<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rhoemetalces III</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 46 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rhoemetalces III was the last king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thrace">Thrace</a>, a Roman client ruler of the Sapaean house. The emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caligula">Caligula</a> made him king of Thrace in 38 CE, at a time when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> governed the region through native princes. He was murdered in 46 CE, and the emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/claudius">Claudius</a> then annexed the kingdom as the province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thracia">Thracia</a>, ending native kingship in Thrace.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rhoemetalces-iii.jpg" alt="Rhoemetalces III" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Johny SYSEL · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rhoemetalkes%2B.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
